{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:ParseQuantity","summary":"ParseQuantity now caches the canonical string on the returned Quantity in the two non-early return paths, since String() no longer caches. Parsed quantities keep their cached string for later encoding.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"ParseQuantity now caches canonical string before returning","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Changes what state parsed Quantity values carry (unexported s), affecting equality, encoding cost and data-race behavior across the API machinery.","risk_signals":["public API behavior","shared type used widely","reflect.DeepEqual sensitivity"],"focus":["Every return path in ParseQuantity sets q.s (early '0' and canonical-input paths already did)","Callers that compare parsed Quantities with reflect.DeepEqual against constructed ones"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).String","summary":"String() no longer writes the computed string back to the receiver; it returns the cached value if present, otherwise computes without caching. This removes a data race on concurrent reads but makes quantities built without ParseQuantity recompute on each call.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Quantity.String no longer mutates receiver or caches result","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Removes a side effect of a widely used method, changing concurrency behavior and performance of encoding paths.","risk_signals":["concurrency","performance on encoding hot paths","side-effect removal"],"focus":["Quantities created via NewQuantity/NewMilliQuantity/math ops now recompute String on each call in JSON/proto marshaling","Code or tests that relied on String() populating q.s (DeepEqual comparisons)"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).CacheString","summary":"Adds a new exported method that computes the canonical string and stores it on the receiver, for callers that own the instance. It always writes, so racy use is detected by the race detector.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add exported Quantity.CacheString that stores canonical string","confidence":0.85,"reason":"New public API method that mutates the receiver, with concurrency contract the caller must honor.","risk_signals":["public API","mutating method","concurrency"],"focus":["Unconditional write q.s = q.String() on an already-cached instance can race for shared instances","Nil receiver returns \"<nil>\" consistent with String"]},
